# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  apps/mobile — Expo environment
#
#  Copy to `.env` for local development.
#
#  IMPORTANT: every EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable is inlined into the JS bundle at build
#  time and is readable by anyone with the APK. Only ever put public values here —
#  no secrets, no API keys. The Google *client IDs* below are public by design;
#  the client *secret* lives only in apps/api/.env.
#
#  Values for an EAS build come from the `env` block of the matching profile in
#  eas.json (or from EAS environment variables), not from this file.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Backend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the Next.js API in apps/api is reachable.
#
#   Android emulator          → http://10.0.2.2:3000
#   Physical phone, same wifi  → http://<your-laptop-lan-ip>:3000
#   Production (Phase 11)      → https://api.yourdomain.in
#
# A physical device cannot reach `localhost` — that resolves to the phone itself.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL="http://10.0.2.2:3000"

# Seconds before an API request is abandoned. Parking gates often have weak
# signal, so this is generous on purpose.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_TIMEOUT_SECONDS="20"

# ── Google Sign-In (Phase 02, decisions.md D3) ──────────────────────────────
# The "Web application" OAuth client ID from Google Cloud Console. Counter-
# intuitively this is what a native app passes to request an ID token, because
# the backend needs a token whose audience it can verify.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=""

# The "Android" OAuth client ID (package name + the SHA-1 of the EAS signing key).
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=""

# ── EAS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Written by `eas init`; read by app.config.ts and required by expo-notifications
# to obtain an Expo push token (Phase 09).
EAS_PROJECT_ID=""
